{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Casting Whispers",
    "steam_appid": 2406880,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2406880/extras/fe1000d57bf781b1d61d9bff1ee8fffe.avif?t=1754338955\" /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your mentor was always a private man, but he was also always there for you. Tonight, however, he seems unwell. In the old industrial\u00a0city of Corburgh, Connecticut, there are many urban legends. Myths from the 1930s and 40s. It's 1961 and you're a lab assistant in the exciting new field of parapsychology.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Go to the professor's apartment, find out what's wrong, and survive the sinister secret under your nose. The ghosts of the city's past haunt the residents. The past never truly dies; it merely echoes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use your ears to listen for it...</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Casting Whispers is a first-person psychological horror game where you will need to use both sight and sound to keep yourself safe and further your investigation. You will need to close your eyes in-game to listen for clues in the environment, and keep a wary ear open for small changes in your environment. Things are not as they may seem and your senses may lie to you...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2406880/extras/42cd154ee33e94da70782e6a379dcff9.avif?t=1754338955\" /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Listening Mechanic</strong><br>Use more than sight to navigate your environment. Press and hold the Listen key to close your eyes and focus on your ears. Use this to eavesdrop on conversations through doors, listen for hidden mechanisms, or hear things where you cannot see them.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Unique Threat</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The danger in 1195 Norman Ave has managed to remain hidden in the middle of a populated city somehow. Avoid it and confront it.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Grounded Investigation</strong><br>Explore the various mysteries of 1195 Norman Ave to piece together a more complete image of what's going on. There are large elements of the mystery that can be missed, context not acquired, if you are not thorough.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Linear Narrative (with some variations)</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enjoy a linear story with multiple endings, some of which aren't obvious. Parts of Casting Whispers will actually play out a little differently based on both chance and your choices.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>6-8 hrs of content</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Solving the mystery, surviving the unique threat, and exploring the space; with some small easter eggs as well.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Unique Historical Setting</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It is 1961 in a fictional American city on the east coast. The 1950s are starting to fade into the 60s. It is an exciting time of possibilities, but also a time trying to ignore the sins of the past and pretend they aren't still happening...</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Special Thanks</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Casting Whispers</strong>\u00a0has been a proud indie project, done by a solo-developer and fully voiced by union talent. I could not have made this without the help of those who gave advice and collaborated, and it was a joy to make.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2406880/extras/fe1000d57bf781b1d61d9bff1ee8fffe.avif?t=1754338955\" /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your mentor was always a private man, but he was also always there for you. Tonight, however, he seems unwell. In the old industrial\u00a0city of Corburgh, Connecticut, there are many urban legends. Myths from the 1930s and 40s. It's 1961 and you're a lab assistant in the exciting new field of parapsychology.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Go to the professor's apartment, find out what's wrong, and survive the sinister secret under your nose. The ghosts of the city's past haunt the residents. The past never truly dies; it merely echoes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use your ears to listen for it...</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Casting Whispers is a first-person psychological horror game where you will need to use both sight and sound to keep yourself safe and further your investigation. You will need to close your eyes in-game to listen for clues in the environment, and keep a wary ear open for small changes in your environment. Things are not as they may seem and your senses may lie to you...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2406880/extras/42cd154ee33e94da70782e6a379dcff9.avif?t=1754338955\" /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Listening Mechanic</strong><br>Use more than sight to navigate your environment. Press and hold the Listen key to close your eyes and focus on your ears. Use this to eavesdrop on conversations through doors, listen for hidden mechanisms, or hear things where you cannot see them.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Unique Threat</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The danger in 1195 Norman Ave has managed to remain hidden in the middle of a populated city somehow. Avoid it and confront it.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Grounded Investigation</strong><br>Explore the various mysteries of 1195 Norman Ave to piece together a more complete image of what's going on. There are large elements of the mystery that can be missed, context not acquired, if you are not thorough.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Linear Narrative (with some variations)</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enjoy a linear story with multiple endings, some of which aren't obvious. Parts of Casting Whispers will actually play out a little differently based on both chance and your choices.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>6-8 hrs of content</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Solving the mystery, surviving the unique threat, and exploring the space; with some small easter eggs as well.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Unique Historical Setting</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It is 1961 in a fictional American city on the east coast. The 1950s are starting to fade into the 60s. It is an exciting time of possibilities, but also a time trying to ignore the sins of the past and pretend they aren't still happening...</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Special Thanks</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Casting Whispers</strong>\u00a0has been a proud indie project, done by a solo-developer and fully voiced by union talent. I could not have made this without the help of those who gave advice and collaborated, and it was a joy to make.</p>",
    "short_description": "Investigate and uncover a sinister past under your very nose. Close your eyes and listen for clues using a unique Listening mechanic. Question your senses. Survive.",
